{"id":"20260825T232130.639288273Z-317650c6","time":"2026-08-25T23:21:30.639288273Z","session_id":"session-20260825T231838.982866090Z","task_id":"task-1787699918983209064","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  Scrolling the transcript responds only to PgUp/PgDn, which terminals and multiplexers routinely capture for their own scrollback before the program sees it, and a single-line scroll is undone immediately so the keys appear dead.\n\nMake scrolling respond to what a reader actually reaches for: the arrow keys, the usual ctrl bindings, and the mouse wheel. One notch must move exactly one line and must not be clamped back. Scrolling down must move towards the newest output, and the transcript must keep reporting how many earlier lines are hidden. How the position is stored is yours to decide.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] Model.Update currently sends key presses through transcript scrolling before menu and composer handling, while Model.scroll recognizes PgUp, PgDn, Shift+Up, Shift+Down, and Ctrl+G. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Rendering clamps a local top row, but scrollPosition uses a different height approximation and does not clamp a stored scrollTop above the rendered maximum, allowing reverse one-line movement to appear ineffective. (internal/tui/model.go transcript viewport) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The current view reserves a transcript row for a note that reports how many earlier lines are hidden. (internal/tui/model.go transcript rendering) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The current checkout has no transcript-scrolling regression test file. (internal/tui/scroll_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei directly anchors the critical provider-credential ownership invariant to internal/tui/model.go, so this slice must avoid the provider login and authentication path. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: graph\n  [NEEDS EVIDENCE] Ctrl+P and Ctrl+N are the intended conventional Ctrl aliases for one-line up and down navigation. (transcript input bindings) — source: inference\n  [NEEDS EVIDENCE] Bubble Tea's configured v2 dependency can deliver mouse-wheel events when the view enables mouse reporting. (TUI mouse input) — source: inference\n  [evidence-bearing] Repository verification requires formatting cmd and internal, then running go vet and the complete Go test suite. (repository verification) — source: repository\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: human-authority-required\n"}
